śárman, n.
 —1. cover; protection; shelter;
 refuge;
 —2. comfort, joy;
 —3.
common at the end of Brahman-names,
19^11, 42^11, 59^13N. [see under śaraṇa.]

sarít, f. stream. [√sṛ, ‘run, flow,’ 383. 3:
for mg, cf. Ger. Fluss, ‘stream,’ w. fliessen,
‘flow,’ and Eng. stream under √sru.]

sárga, m.
 —1. shot;
 —2. stream or spurt
or jet;
 —3. a letting loose;
 —4. that
which is let loose, esp. a herd let loose
from the stall, 76^4;
 —5. chapter of an
epic poem, a fig. use of the word in mg 1
or 2. [√sṛj, 216. 1.]
